]
Thus all Möbius-bearing factors in (2) lie in the single carrier P<Q^a, while at least two fixed-power unweighted factors remain outside that carrier.

This is an algebraic identity and factor-anatomy theorem. It makes no analytic estimate for the HB-nonsplittable representations and no assertion that a tuple-dependent choice of a subset produces separated coefficient arrays.

512b50816bb8e5ef.proof:
Define the arithmetic function
[
 M_z(r)=mu(r){ f1}_{rle z}
]
and write (*) for Dirichlet convolution, ({ f1}(r)=1) for every positive integer r, and (delta_1) for the convolution identity. Put
[
