 =-{1\over H_P}\sum_\rho\eta_\rho
 \sum_{q\asymp Q}
 \mu(q){\bf1}_{(q,g)=1}A_\rho(q)
 \langle{\bf M}_{\rho,q,g},{\bf H}_{\rho,q,g}\rangle_q .
 }                                                               \tag{6}
\]
Thus the reciprocal-modulus Möbius sign \(\mu(q)\), the long sign \(\mu(m)\), every exact \(g\)-gate, the full \(h,t\) source packet, the possibly nonunit target \(A\), and the same character coordinate are all retained. Formula (6) is not a sum of independent character estimates.

The joint source-vector norm has the exact unit-supported Farey-transform identity
\[
 \boxed{
 \|{\bf H}_{\rho,q,g}\|_2^2
 ={1\over\varphi(q)}
 \sum_{x\pmod q}^{*}
 \left|
 \sum_{\substack{F\le |h|<2F\\T\le t<2T\\(t,qg)=1}}
 E_\rho(h)D_\rho(t)e_q(Axh\overline t)
 \right|^2 .
 }                                                               \tag{7}
\]
The long-vector norm is the exact signed progression covariance
\[
 \boxed{
 \begin{aligned}
 \|{\bf M}_{\rho,q,g}\|_2^2
 =\varphi(q)
 \sum_{\substack{m_1,m_2\asymp M\\
                  m_1\equiv m_2\pmod q\\
                  (m_1m_2,qg)=1}}
 &\mu(m_1)\mu(m_2)\\
 &\times C_\rho(m_1)\overline{C_\rho(m_2)} .
 \end{aligned}
 }                                                               \tag{8}
\]
Consequently the smallest literal fixed-\(g\) analytic supplier on this route is
\[
 \boxed{
 {1\over H_P}\left|
 \sum_\rho\eta_\rho
 \sum_{q\asymp Q}
 \mu(q){\bf1}_{(q,g)=1}A_\rho(q)
