\]
for some fixed \(\delta_U>0\), uniformly over the literal projective boxes, with their total \(x^{o(1)}\) coefficient mass. This estimate would pay the complete ULTRA-LONG-MU-\(N\) family after the standard outer-\(g\) sum.

Neither ULTRA-MU-VECTOR nor a bound for either vector norm is asserted here. Applying Cauchy--Schwarz separately for every \(q\), followed by triangle inequality in \(q\), deletes the signed squarefree cross-\(q\) coefficient \(\mu(q)\); it is therefore not the supplier stated above. No existing independent-character second-moment estimate is imported. This theorem is the exact source-specific vector handoff only; it proves no ENDPOINT-DIAGONAL-\(N\), critical-tail, post-\(A\), or Goldbach conclusion.

