Thus the five resulting classes—interval prime, stopping composite, and one, two, or three rough primes—cover every (r) satisfying (1)-(2) exactly and preserve (mu(r)).

6414b11506a84ff0.proof:
Suppose first that (j=j_I(r)>0). For every interval prime (pmid r), squarefreeness gives
[
