Put (T_easymp U/e) and (S_easymp Y/e). After division by (H), expand the two fourth-root sums in the bound of fact (73fb9efe1286f7e9). Using (3), equivalently (Uasymp_C QH/Y), the four terms for a fixed (e), apart from a common epsilon factor and (	au_J(e)^2), are bounded by
