d399d1df6821854c.proof:
We verify that every step of fact 76040270e1ddf949 applies under the displayed separated-outer hypothesis.

In the proof of fact 76040270e1ddf949, the condition that every prime divisor of the outer variable is at most L is used only in its opening comparison with the final prime, in order to conclude gcd(v,p)=1. The present statement assumes that conclusion directly for every supported pair. From that point onward, the proof uses only:
(1) V<=S_0, hence log V/log Q<=2beta-2+3sigma+O(1/log Q);
(2) the divisor bound on xi_v;
(3) the prime-indicator identity Lambda/log minus proper prime powers;
(4) the exact Vaughan decomposition of fact 29c43cef40f2e79b;
(5) the beta_1 slot inequalities rederived in fact 76040270e1ddf949;
(6) the actual-frequency correlated ledger of fact 42720f6d803c4640;
(7) the multiplier-one Type-I estimate of fact bbcb9f66597c667c;
and (8) the displayed arbitrary fixed-order Fourier decay.

None of steps (1)-(8) factors v or uses an upper bound on its prime divisors. When v is grouped with a Vaughan factor l, the coefficient at s=vl is divisor-bounded because
sum_{vl=s}tau_J(v)tau_K(l)log(2P)<=tau_{J+K+2}(s)log(2P)
after increasing the fixed order. The proper-prime-power error uses only V<=S_0 and is exactly the bound
O(Q^epsilon sum_F |omega_F|(F/H_P) Q(VB)^(1/2))
=O(Q^(9/5-2sigma))
from fact 76040270e1ddf949.

For completeness, on an actual frequency block put u_F=F/H_P. Every correlated Vaughan box is placed in
H_T^2Q^(3sigma)<=S<=Q^(1-3sigma)/H_T^2.
Fact 42720f6d803c4640 then gives the four baseline savings of fact 76040270e1ddf949, with only G^(1/4)u_F^(3/4) on the first two and u_F on the last two. The sums of |omega_F|u_F^(3/4) and |omega_F|u_F are bounded. The short Type-I coefficient scale is at most Q^(1/2-3sigma); fact bbcb9f66597c667c applies on polynomial F with target A and no modulus-dependent unit, and larger F is paid absolutely by the same Fourier decay. These arguments prove O(GQ^(2-delta_1)) for G>=1 and O(Q^(2-delta_2)) on the near-balanced strip exactly as in the accepted proof.

Thus replacing smooth-prime support by the explicit separated-outer condition changes no analytic step, coefficient norm, frequency normalization, target condition, or saving. This proves both assertions and all stated uniformity.

