\]
where \(d_{p,t_y}\) is the exact coefficient in fact
\(97b9d86408362df2\). Set
\[
 A_{p,k,X}(r,H,\tau)
 =\sum_{\lambda\in\Lambda_{p,k,X}(r,H,\tau)}
 |a_{p,\lambda}|,                                             \tag{7}
\]
\[
 U_{p,k,X}(r)
 =\sum_{H\in\mathbb F_p^\times}
 \max_{\tau\in\mathbb F_p^\times}
 A_{p,k,X}(r,H,\tau),                                         \tag{8}
\]
and
\[
 Y_{p,k,X}
 =L_{p,k}^2\sum_{r\in\mathbb F_p}U_{p,k,X}(r)^2.              \tag{9}
\]
Then, uniformly in \(p,k,X,r,H,\tau\), for every \(\varepsilon>0\),
\[
 \boxed{
 A_{p,k,X}(r,H,\tau)
 \ll_\varepsilon Q^\varepsilon\left(1+{Q\over p}\right).
 }                                                             \tag{10}
\]
Consequently
\[
 \boxed{
 U_{p,k,X}(r)
 \ll_\varepsilon Q^\varepsilon F
 \left(1+{Q\over p}\right),
 }                                                             \tag{11}
\]
and
\[
 \boxed{
 Y_{p,k,X}
 \ll_\varepsilon Q^\varepsilon
 L_{p,k}^2\min(p,2Q)F^2
 \left(1+{Q\over p}\right)^2.
 }                                                             \tag{12}
\]
For fixed \(p,X\), summing (12) over all deterministic blocks of fact
\(ec8a0fbdab03cda6\) gives
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_kY_{p,k,X}
 \ll_\varepsilon Q^\varepsilon
 B\min(p,2Q)F^2
 \left(1+{Q\over p}\right)^2.
 }                                                             \tag{13}
\]

The vector \(v(a)=(a,\overline a)\in\mathbb C^2\) and the complex four-linear coordinate-selection contraction from fact \(97b9d86408362df2\) retain the residual CRT phases and give vector norm \(\|v(a)\|=|a|\). Hence (7)-(9) are literal instances of the \(A_p,U_p,Y_p\) envelope slots in facts \(a84f95a82329a894\), \(bbd687d016ee3ff6\), and \(ec8a0fbdab03cda6\), conditional on the separate common-\(X\) completion and any additional remaining-face operator.

This theorem removes the \(u\)-twist from the occupancy variables by using \(T=n/p\), but it does not prove that the complete literal coefficient has the separated bounded-variation form required by fact \(9ea2dddfbbbd191a\). It also does not construct the common-\(X\) completion, compare \(\sum_{p,k}Y_{p,k,X}\) with the complete joint-completion Hilbert norm, pay \(p\le2F\), short blocks, small selected primes, or distinct-prime cross terms, and proves neither TOP-B-BALG-DEEP-NR-SPEC, POST-A-TAIL, nor Goldbach.

