end{array}                                                  	ag{14}
]
The Archimedean phase
[
 e!left(- rac{A	au}{ab,u_1u_2}ight)                  	ag{15}
]
is retained in every stratum. In particular, (	au=0) is retained in the last row and gives the arithmetic diagonal (u_1=u_2).

Because each (u_j) is a squarefree product of its two canonical distinct primes, the original pair support is the disjoint union of:
[
