]
It retains the q-residue projectors, (12), (15), all four strata in (14), all three collision classes in (16), the reciprocal envelope and every literal mask.

The residue energy in equation (22) of fact 70f0948e686a21c8 is an exact expansion of the same-residue pair support, but it is not exactly equivalent to (17). The passage from the linear residue row
[
 sum_v Q(v)S(v)                                            	ag{18}
]
to (sum_v|S(v)|^2) uses Cauchy--Schwarz and gives only the sufficient estimate (23) of that fact. Algebraically, when there is more than one unit residue, (18) is one linear functional of the residue vector S whereas the energy is its full squared norm; a nonzero linear functional has a nontrivial kernel. This observation is not a counterexample to the literal E11 source. It shows only that an energy theorem is a sufficient stronger supplier and cannot be called an exact reformulation without an additional literal lower comparison. No such lower comparison is asserted. No E11 closure, PMD, C2, DCE or Goldbach conclusion is claimed.
